{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#rem:dc-ch7-3-4","title":"rem:dc-ch7-3-4","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":602,"body":"","kind":"other","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#rem:dc-ch7-3-4","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"rem:dc-ch7-3-4","line":1055,"source":"\\begin{remark}[poles]\n\n  \\label{rem:dc-ch7-3-4}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo, lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction, lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics, lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:3.4}\nA point $p$ of a complete Riemannian manifold is a \\emph{pole} if no point along any geodesic from $p$ is conjugate to $p$. Nonpositive sectional curvature implies that every point is a pole. If a complete simply connected manifold has a pole, then it is diffeomorphic to $\\mathbb{R}^n$.\n\\end{remark}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Remark</div></section>[poles] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-72656d3a64632d6368372d332d34\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-expmap-global\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:3.4</span></span>A point <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> of a complete Riemannian manifold is a <em>pole</em> if no point along any geodesic from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> is conjugate to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>. Nonpositive sectional curvature implies that every point is a pole. If a complete simply connected manifold has a pole, then it is diffeomorphic to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathbb {R}^n$\">$\\mathbb {R}^n$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-5-minimizing","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#rem:dc-ch7-3-4","title":"rem:dc-ch7-3-4","tex":"\\begin{remark}[poles]\n\n  \\label{rem:dc-ch7-3-4}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo, lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction, lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics, lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-global}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:3.4}\nA point $p$ of a complete Riemannian manifold is a \\emph{pole} if no point along any geodesic from $p$ is conjugate to $p$. Nonpositive sectional curvature implies that every point is a pole. If a complete simply connected manifold has a pole, then it is diffeomorphic to $\\mathbb{R}^n$.\n\\end{remark}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-pole-diffeo","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-ray-reduction","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-4-rays-are-geodesics","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-exp